        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The Old Mill Property is a unique and attractive property situated just a short walk from the village of Ballycastle in North Mayo. Set on an impressive c. 2.8-acre site, the property offers a rare combination of a comfortable family home, extensive grounds and significant potential for further development, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\nThe original house was built circa 1935 and was subsequently extended in the 1990s. The property is in good condition and has benefited from considerable upgrading and modernisation works over the past 10–12 years.\r\n\r\nImprovements include rewiring and replumbing, a new oil-fired heating system, and the installation of a new solid-fuel stove with back boiler. The original section of the house has also been insulated and wrapped, improving its energy efficiency and comfort.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation currently comprises an entrance porch, living room, sitting room, kitchen/dining area, utility room, three bedrooms, one of which is en-suite, main bathroom and guest WC. The sitting room was originally the fourth bedroom and could potentially be reinstated, subject to the buyer's requirements.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property benefits from a large shed together with the remains of the historic Old Mill and associated outbuildings. These substantial structures provide an exciting opportunity for the new owner. With extensive renovation and subject to planning permission and any other required consents, they may have potential for use as a workshop, studio, ancillary accommodation or other suitable purposes.\r\n\r\nThe extensive grounds provide excellent space and privacy and would appeal to a wide variety of purchasers, including those seeking a family home, hobby farm, smallholding, workshop space or a property with scope for future development.\r\n\r\nThe roof of the house requires some attention and repair, but overall the property has been well maintained and substantially upgraded in recent years.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\nEntrance Porch\r\nLiving Room\r\nSitting Room / Former Bedroom 4\r\nKitchen / Dining Area\r\nUtility Room\r\n3 Bedrooms\r\nEn-suite Bedroom\r\nMain Bathroom\r\nGuest WC\r\nOutside Shed\r\nOld Mill Ruins and Outbuildings\r\nLocation\r\nBallycastle is a picturesque coastal village in North Mayo, located approximately 26 km from Ballina and forming part of the Wild Atlantic Way. The area is renowned for its spectacular Atlantic coastline, beaches, archaeological heritage and unspoilt rural landscape.\r\n\r\nNearby attractions include Downpatrick Head, with its dramatic cliffs and famous Dún Briste sea stack, Ballycastle Beach, and the internationally significant Céide Fields, a Neolithic landscape dating back almost 6,000 years.\r\n\r\nThe wider area offers an exceptional range of outdoor and recreational opportunities, including coastal walks, beaches, fishing, surfing and access to some of North Mayo's most scenic countryside.\r\n\r\nA Property Full of Potential\r\nThe Old Mill Property represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial property in a beautiful coastal location, with c. 2.8 acres of land and a collection of historic mill buildings and outbuildings.\r\n\r\nWhile requiring some further work, particularly to the roof, the property has already benefited from significant investment and upgrading. The combination of the existing house, extensive site and historic Old Mill buildings gives this property considerable scope for those looking for something beyond an ordinary residential property.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the location, character, scale and potential of this unique property."
